// Every query rejects back faces of one-sided surfaces ((state.w&4)==0 below).
// With hardware face culling (target.z bit 2) one-sided instances enable
// facing culling in the TLAS and this flag culls exactly those back faces in
// traversal (same front-face definition), so their surfaces can be opaque.
// Diagnostics (rtx.native.pathtrace.traversalDebug; wrong images): target.z
